In `sync_example.go`, inside the `for` loop in `benchmarkLargeSizePool`, insert code to clear the `dataLarge` slice before it is returned to the pool. This prevents leaking data between uses of the pooled slice.

```go
// old
		_ = dataLarge
		bytePool.Put(dataLarge)

// new
		_ = dataLarge
		// Zero out the buffer before putting it back to the pool to avoid data leaks.
		for i := range dataLarge {
			dataLarge[i] = 0
		}
		bytePool.Put(dataLarge)
```

