In `sync_example.go`, modify the benchmark loop to use a local variable instead of the global `dataLarge`. This makes the benchmark safe to run in parallel.

```go
// old
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
		dataLarge = bytePool.Get().([]byte)
		_ = dataLarge
		bytePool.Put(dataLarge)
	}

// new
	for i := 0; i < b.N; i++ {
		data := bytePool.Get().([]byte)
		_ = data
		bytePool.Put(data)
	}
```

